Q4 (Teams, Onkar's own point): "Tandem AUTO — what if something comes in the middle, or treatment is discontinued between the two?"

Today the engine works like this: a new drug (or a donor transplant or CAR-T) between the two transplants breaks the pair — the second transplant starts its own line. But treatment simply running out or stopping between them does not break the pair — the line is held open to the second transplant.

In the data this is small: the stop-between-transplants shape is 9 cases and the drug-in-between shape is 13. So whichever way you decide, few patients move — but we'd like your confirmation that the current reading is what you want. The worked examples are S10 and S11 in the scenario workbook.

